{"kind":"assert","text":"Amendment to H1 (99918e60), 27 October. Two changes.\n\n1. The condition \"never ahead of the grow demo slices of plan 033\" is lifted. Order now: after G1 (host none, filed today), before the standing release items and plan 033's G4. The first condition (the design note approved) is met.\n\n2. One item added, from the launchd and HTTPS validation e6a5cd22 (item 2): behind a local proxy the Worker sees http:// URLs, and hosted MCP agent creation is refused 403 (packages/mcp/src/hosted.ts:148, rule `service`) because the service is url.origin. Fix: one nonsecret setting `PUBLIC_ORIGIN`, the deployment's origin as clients see it. Where set, it replaces url.origin for identity: the hosted MCP service (hosted.ts:148, 305), the applications route's deployment default (packages/scope/src/applications/route.ts:63) and demo creation's origin checks (apps/room/demo-creation.ts). Unset keeps url.origin. No reading of X-Forwarded-Proto or any forwarded header for identity; the proxy owns only CF-Connecting-IP as today. Witness: with http between proxy and Worker and the setting present, agent create answers 201 and the MCP session runs; without the setting, 403 as now; a request whose Host differs from the setting is not special-cased.\n\nAlso in H1's celld project: /health answers the real storage readiness (the stand-in entry answered 503 in the validation). The validation's served Caddyfile and launchd parameters are H3's input, not H1's.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}